# Project Context (ALWAYS FOLLOW)

Full contract: `AGENTS.md`. Knowledge base: `.claude/kb/INDEX.md` (read it, then the doc for the area you touch).

## Stack and constraints
- Luna playable ad. Unity 6 + URP, **Leopotam EcsLite** (embedded in `Assets/LeoEcs`). No Zenject, no UniTask, no addressables.
- Gameplay stays data-oriented: components are structs, systems hold behavior, `GameBootstrap` owns the worlds and the system list.
- Do not add third-party packages unless asked: Luna build size and compatibility are the limit.
- Code may be converted to JS by Luna: no reflection, async/threads, `ref` returns, `foreach` over filters, LINQ in hot paths.

## Output discipline
- Small, compile-safe steps. For a large change propose a plan, then implement step 1-2 only.
- Never invent APIs or classes that are not in the repo; ask for the exact file if context is missing.
- Preserve existing naming, folder structure and patterns. Minimal diff; no drive-by reformatting.
- No comments that narrate the code; short ones only for Luna footguns or a non-obvious "why".

## Performance
- Cache pools and filters in `Init`; no allocations in `Run`; raw dense/sparse array access with bounds and `idx <= 0` checks (see `.claude/kb/01-conventions.md`).
- No per-frame string building or log spam.

## System ordering
- Do not reorder systems in `GameBootstrap.BindSystems` unless the task requires it. When adding a system, state which events/components it needs from earlier systems
  and what later systems expect (`.claude/kb/02-gameplay-ecs.md`, "System order").
- Every system has a public `(GameContext ctx)` constructor; new tunables are a serialized field on `GameBootstrap` plus a `GameContext` parameter/property.

## Namespaces
- ECS code uses `Playeble.Scripts.Gameplay.<Feature>` (Dragon, Movements, ReelSlots, Selection) - keep the "Playeble" spelling.
- Views/enums in `Assets/!Project/Scripts` use `AzurGames.Wool.*`; Luna template scripts use `Azur.Playable*`; editor tools `Playeble.EditorTools`.
- Match the namespace of the neighbouring files in the same folder.

## Scenes
- Four scenes share `GameBootstrap` (`Playable_3`, `Playable_4`, `Template`, `Template_2`); only `Playable_3` is in the Luna export (`luna.json`).
  A new serialized field needs a default that keeps the other scenes working.
